# Review ownership for docs.extole.com.
#
# A merge to `main` publishes the live customer site, and `validate` only proves the site
# builds: a page absent from `docs.json` ships unreachable, and nothing mechanical checks
# terminology, placement, or whether a claim about the product is true. Those are a
# reviewer's, so the docs owner is requested on every change that reaches a reader.
#
# GitHub requests a code owner when a pull request opens ready, or when a draft is marked
# ready for review -- not while it is a draft.

# Everything customer-visible, plus the navigation and the standards that govern it.
/guides/      @ekthayer
/product/     @ekthayer
/technical/   @ekthayer
/news/        @ekthayer
/runbooks/    @ekthayer
/images/      @ekthayer
/docs.json    @ekthayer
/url-map.json @ekthayer
/index.mdx    @ekthayer
/.mintlify/   @ekthayer

# Left unowned on purpose: `api-reference/*.json` are OpenAPI bundles written by CI from
# `extole/openapi`, and Mintlify generates the whole API Reference tab from them. Owning
# them would request a review on every sync -- 20 of them in the four weeks to 2026-09-21 --
# for a diff no human hand-edits. `AGENTS.md`, `.agents/` and `.github/` are also left
# unowned: they are agent and CI configuration rather than pages a customer reads.
